The legal text is the Constitution of the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, 52 titles of the Pennsylvania Consolidated Statutes, and six unconsolidated statutes, as published by the Pennsylvania General Assembly (Legislative Data Processing Center) at https://www.palegis.us/statutes/ .

The General Assembly claims no copyright in the text. Its Legal Notices say only that the site is an information service whose
content does not replace the official versions. Statute text of a state is not copyrightable: Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org,
Inc., 590 U.S. 255 (2020). Only statute text is taken; the annotations of the unofficial Purdon's Pennsylvania Statutes (West) are
a separate work and are not used. The text is republished here with credit to the Pennsylvania General Assembly as its publisher.

The arrangement of this repository, its tables, commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and may be reused under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This repository is not legal advice
and not an official publication.
